    "result_text": "The three files are the base harness, an audit-log helper, and the single `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 so all tests ran and passed. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `selfLink` on the owner API representation, returning `/api/owners/` followed by the owner's id.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `id`), so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a small `selfLink(Owner)` default method that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`.\n\nThis follows the existing pattern for the mapper's other derived fields (one small single-responsibility default method per computed field) rather than duplicating the URL logic. Because both the GET responder (`RespondWithOwner`) and the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) already build the DTO via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, no YAML/function-chain changes were needed and `selfLink` now appears on every owner response.\n\nThe full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the new `coreReturnsSelfLink` acceptance test.",
